{
  "meta": {
    "description": "Shared contract for the exoplanet simulator physics. Any implementation, in any language, is correct only if it reproduces every case here. The JavaScript suite in physics.test.js reads this file; a Python notebook can read the same file and check its own implementation against it.",
    "tolerance_note": "relTol is fractional (0.02 = 2%). absTol is in the natural units of the quantity. Give one or the other.",
    "call_schema": "call.fn is a top-level function name. call.args is the argument list; a single object argument is passed as a one-element array. expect.path indexes into the returned value with dots and integers, e.g. 'conservative.0' or 'tempsC.45'. Omit path when the return value is itself a number.",
    "grid_note": "Latitude and substellar-angle arrays run -90 to +90 in 2-degree steps, so index 0 = -90, index 45 = 0, index 90 = +90."
  },
  "cases": [
